If the TFile dies and we still need the root histogram, won't be able to access it any longer. 

This is why calling a separate function with TString filename and asking it to open up the file and read it and return the 
histo caused the histo to not be usable afterwards when we came out of the function. 

TIP: Don't pass around TString filenames, open up the TFile in the home directory and take out the histograms from it

PREVENTS MEMORY CRASH:
H means histogram and 1 means 1D. This command means not to attach the new histograms to the current ROOT directory to manage. ROOT
automatically attaches the newly created histograms to the current ROOT directory to manage. This command disables that.

TH1::AddDirectory(false); 
